 **Lemma (frozen witnesses).** Under the modified definition, let $\vec X=\vec x$ be a cause of $\varphi$ with a witness in which no variable violates its equation. Then every member of $\vec X$ is a root, and $\varphi$ depends counterfactually on $\vec X=\vec x$.
 
-*Proof.* Under AC2(a$^m$), the frozen variables keep their actual values. A non-descendant of $\vec X$ has only non-descendants as parents, so by induction every non-descendant of $\vec X$ takes its actual value in the witness world. An endogenous member of $\vec X$ therefore has its actual parent values, and its equation returns its actual value, not the counterfactual value the witness assigns it; so it violates its equation. If all members of $\vec X$ are roots and no frozen variable violates its equation, each frozen variable takes the value its equation gives. The witness world is then the solution under $[\vec X\leftarrow\vec x']$ alone, so $\varphi$ fails under that intervention. ∎
